  "abstract_summary": "Procedural memory in multi-agent large language model (LLM) systems typically caches reusable multi-step action sequences, or skills, indexed by surface task features within a single task domain. This domain-siloed indexing leaves structurally transferable skills invisible to retrieval whenever a new task falls outs...",
